\id INT
\periph New Testament Introduction|id="intnt"

\mt1 A Message from the Translator

\p Welcome to the all-new, 2026 release of the English Majority Text Version of the New Testament, released here once again as The Annotated EMTV New Testament.
\p The 2026 release includes minor updates as well as some miscellaneous typos corrected, both to my translation, and to the footnotes on the bottom of the page.
\p Other annotations are: Italicized text represents words added by the translator. Also, SMALL CAPS represent Old Testament quotations.
\p I firmly believe that what you hold in your hands is the closest representation to the original autographs of the New Testament, by having a translation that has its origins in the Byzantine Text form.
\p What makes this version different from the others, or why have a ‘Majority Text’ Bible translation? It is a good thing that you and I compare these different translations of His word, in our quest to know Him better. For God has declared, “My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge.” (Hosea 4:6)
\p I will point out that the Byzantine Majority Text Manuscripts are the time-tested, trusted manuscripts that were all this world knew for some 1500 years. These manuscripts were used by Erasmus, Luther, the forty-seven scholars who translated the King James Bible, the Geneva Bible, as well as all the reformers, who refused to use the Latin Vulgate.
\p Some 500 years ago, when the first printed text was made, it was no coincidence that God had provided these manuscripts, because these are time-tested, faithful Greek manuscripts, that more accurately represent the original autographs.
\p This translation, the EMTV, is the reading of the “majority” of those same Byzantine Manuscripts that are in existence. Only, instead of the eight or so trustworthy manuscripts that were available in the 1500’s, we have hundreds!
\p To me, the word of God is the only “pure” constant of the universe.
\q1 “Every word of God is pure;
\q1 He is a shield to those who put their trust in Him.
\q1 Do not add to His words,
\q1 Lest He rebuke you, and you be found a liar.” (Prov 30:5-6)
\p It is my prayer that this work will bring honor to our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, and to our God and Father.
\p Peace of Christ upon you all as you study the Father’s word.
\p In His Service,
\p Paul W. Esposito, Th.D.
\b
\b
\mt1 About the Author
\p I cannot for a moment take one ounce of credit for this great Book, this Bible translation.
\p All the credit goes to Almighty God, and to His Son Jesus Christ, who Himself is the living embodiment of the word of God.
\p This Book is God’s word to mankind. Included in its pages is the key of life:
\li1 1. How to have peace with God.
\li1 2. How to stand before Him on Judgment Day, and to be accepted in the Beloved.
\p It’s my prayer that this Bible would be a blessing in your life.
\p May the peace of Jesus Christ be imparted to your soul this day!
\p Pastor Paul W. Esposito, Th.D.